WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:06.253
Samir Ibrahim: Who’s ready for a story?

00:00:06.294 --> 00:00:07.295
Audience: Yes.

00:00:07.295 --> 00:00:08.296
SA: Alright.

00:00:08.713 --> 00:00:13.134
Once upon a time, in a land
very very close to us,

00:00:13.843 --> 00:00:15.178
there was a planet.

00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:17.639
And that planet was on fire.

00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:20.058
But it didn’t start that way.

00:00:20.392 --> 00:00:22.686
Global atmospheric
carbon dioxide concentrations

00:00:22.727 --> 00:00:25.564
in parts per million
for the past 800,000 years

00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:27.649
didn’t exceed 300 parts per million.

00:00:27.899 --> 00:00:30.360
And that peak happened
about 300,000 years ago.

00:00:30.652 --> 00:00:33.446
The annual rate of increase
of atmospheric carbon dioxide

00:00:33.446 --> 00:00:35.031
as measured in parts per...

00:00:35.532 --> 00:00:36.533
oh...

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:38.410
looks like you’ve fallen asleep.

00:00:38.451 --> 00:00:39.661
(Laughter)

00:00:39.869 --> 00:00:43.832
Climate change is the most urgent issue
facing humanity today.

00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:46.835
But telling you a boring story
like I just did

00:00:47.168 --> 00:00:50.422
is not going to create the change we need
to secure a livable future.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.009
We need climate activism to be mainstream.

00:00:54.759 --> 00:00:57.220
We need the fight against
climate change to be cool.

00:00:58.013 --> 00:00:59.514
Let’s try something different.

00:00:59.723 --> 00:01:01.516
Ladies and gentlemen, please welcome

00:01:01.558 --> 00:01:03.226
MyVerse and Kristen Warren.

00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:10.233
(Applause)

00:01:10.984 --> 00:01:17.949
